@* =====================================================================================
   FILE SUMMARY
   What it does: Public landing page (anyone, logged in or not, lands here at "/"). Uses
                 _LandingLayout.cshtml instead of the site-wide _Layout.cshtml — see that
                 file's FILE SUMMARY for why (and for the note on this page being the one
                 Spanish-language exception in the app). The header adapts to whether the
                 visitor is logged in (Dashboard/Log out) or not (Register/Log in), same
                 pattern _Layout.cshtml itself uses. The "Log in"/"Register" buttons are real
                 links to AccountController — the fake JavaScript modals from the original
                 design were removed (they showed a fake success toast without ever calling
                 the API). Ratings/reviews and the "+1,420 specialists connected" counter were
                 removed on purpose — there's no real data behind them yet. The service cards
                 are decorative for now (no Service/booking feature exists yet in the WebApp)
                 — clicking one opens a detail modal and "confirming" just shows a toast;
                 wiring this to a real booking flow is a future task.
   Entities connected: None — this project has no database entities
   Tables related: None
   ===================================================================================== *@
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "ServiGo - Servicios Profesionales a Domicilio";
    Layout = "_LandingLayout";
}

<div class="fixed top-0 left-1/4 w-[600px] h-[600px] bg-glow-1 pointer-events-none rounded-full z-0"></div>
<div class="fixed bottom-0 right-1/4 w-[700px] h-[700px] bg-glow-2 pointer-events-none rounded-full z-0"></div>

<partial name="_LandingHeader" />

